# manufacturer CAD in cad/vendor/ is tracked (decision 2026-09-07: the files are needed outside this checkout);
# they remain licensed downloads, see cad/vendor/README.md

# every CAD output is tracked. The only exception: the raw full station assemblies (120-140 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB
# limit) are tracked as the .zip that build.py writes beside them; the raw .step is regenerated by `python cad/build.py`
cad/station/STEP/station_assembly.step
cad/station/STEP/station_assembly_h.step

# cad/blender/ regenerates its heavy artefacts from the tracked station_assembly.step.zip:
# the tessellated GLB (~35 MB) and the two .blend files (~29 MB each). The scripts, the README and
# the renders are tracked; run step_to_glb.py then build_scene.py to get the rest back.
cad/blender/*.glb
cad/blender/*.blend
cad/blender/*.blend1

__pycache__/
*.pyc
